<section id="about">
  <div class="wrap about">

    <div>

      <div class="eyebrow">About Me</div>

      <h2>
        I simply write the things
        I sometimes cannot say.
      </h2>

    </div>


    <div class="box">

      <p>
        Hi, I’m Sarang.
      </p>

      <p>
        I am not a professional writer. I never planned to become one either.
      </p>

      <p>
        I just started writing because there are many things in life
        that I cannot always say out loud. Sometimes I don't know how
        to explain what I feel. Sometimes I don't want to explain it at all.
      </p>

      <p>
        So, I write.
      </p>

      <p>
        I write about things I see, things I feel, people I meet,
        relationships, memories, silence, disappointment, happiness,
        and the little lessons that life teaches us — sometimes gently,
        and sometimes not.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>Words From Within</strong> started with a simple thought:
      </p>

      <blockquote>
        If I cannot say it, maybe I can write it.
      </blockquote>

      <p>
        Some of the words here may be about my own experiences.
        Some may come from things I have seen or felt. And some may
        simply be thoughts that stayed in my mind for too long.
      </p>

      <p>
        I don't expect every piece to mean something to everyone.
      </p>

      <p>
        But if you ever read something here and think,
        <em>“I have felt this too...”</em>
        then maybe these words were worth writing.
      </p>

      <p>
        Welcome to my little space.
      </p>

      <p>
        — Sarang
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>
</section>